  "id": "COMPOUND:34436 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Lobechinenoid D is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a protein that is a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. All these compounds are implicated in the regulation of CCF-STTG1, a protein that appears to be a downstream target of the sialyltransferase. The evidence suggests a potential pathway where Lobechinenoid D may inhibit the sialyltransferase, thereby affecting CCF-STTG1. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same intermediate suggests that the sialyltransferase may play a critical role in the regulation of CCF-STTG1, and Lobechinenoid D may act as a modulator in this process.",
